      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5ab3ad272b67505f726c2a8f|full_name}: I don't think the change to address the difference between standing and lying down is what's causing this, because you can playspace move up high enough that lying down doesn't trigger a change in animation state (i.e. standing to crouching), but the IK works just fine. So I don't think they made the assumption that one is lying down only if their animation state is also crouching or crawling. This seems to be something different. For one reason or another they are making a check for trackers whenever the animation state changes(i.e. crawling to standing) when such a check should only be done upon avatar loading/recalibration(which is really just loading). \nI doubt they'll look at this much though, considering the very small number of users it affects. I need to do some more testing when I get home from work to see how this is affecting in cases where the trackers are covered, but still transmitting to find some alternate solution that doesn't require wearing the trackers and being wired to batteries all night.\n\nBut yeah, this is one of those things they should let us decide, without forcing it upon us automatically",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
