      "value": "@{5ab3ad272b67505f726c2a8f|full_name}: You are misunderstanding the issue. What is causing the problem I describe is the change in animation state from standing to crawling, or vise versa, when 6 trackers aren't detected. \n\nThat change in animation state is not required in order for the IK system to determine if you are lying down. As I stated. You can playspace up high enough that laying down will not trigger the animation state change, but your IK will still work fine. \n\nI mean, you could be right, but that would mean the devs are doing things in a very silly way. \n\nIn fact, as further proof, myself and two other people slept all night without playspace moving to the ground, and we did not encounter this issue. It wasn't until we woke up and decided to move to the ground that we encountered this issue.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
